// diag_dedupe_survive_reject.lls — the counterweight to diag_dedupe_reject.lls.
//
// De-duplicating loop diagnostics must not be bought by throwing one away.
// Silencing all diagnostics on pass 1 (the obvious way to kill the duplicate)
// makes the error below VANISH: a suppressed checker_error returns before
// setting had_error, and had_error is what stops a failed generic instantiation
// from being queued as if it succeeded -- so pass 2 finds the instance cached,
// never re-checks its body, and Vec(int).get_ref -> &int reaches codegen as
// invalid IR with rc=0.
//
// This file must contain NO OTHER ERROR.  With any earlier diagnostic present,
// had_error is already set when the instantiation is attempted, the instance is
// not cached, pass 2 re-checks it, and the error survives -- masking exactly the
// regression this corpus exists to catch.  (Found by injection: the case
// initially lived at the bottom of diag_dedupe_reject.lls and was silently
// inert there.)
import std.core.vec

def main() {
    Vec(int) v = [1]
    int i = 0
    while i < 1 { v.get_ref(0); i = i + 1 }
}
